    "fix": "Check whether the invoice's line items are meant to exclude tax or a discount that's applied separately to the total - AMOUNT_TOLERANCE in validate.py is only 2 cents, deliberately tight, so it will flag a real (not rounding-error) gap between items and total. Raise the tolerance if your invoices commonly have a legitimate small gap."
  },
  {
    "issue": "Duplicate detection misses near-identical invoice numbers",
    "fix": "normalize_invoice_number() handles whitespace, case, and leading zeros - if your vendors format numbers differently in another way (e.g. 'INV_001' vs 'INV-001'), add that normalization rule to the same function so both detection and any future comparison stay in sync."
  },
  {
    "issue": "Extracted totals don't match the actual invoice",
    "fix": "This is exactly what validate.py's amount_mismatch() check exists to catch - if needs_review is True with 'amount_mismatch' listed, trust the flag and check the PDF by hand rather than the extracted total. If it's happening on every invoice, extract.py's MAX_CHARACTERS may be cutting off a multi-page invoice's totals page before the AI ever sees it."
  }
